Zero-shot NLI baseline on data/claims_dev.jsonl (300 claims)
Model: ynie/roberta-large-snli_mnli_fever_anli_R1_R2_R3-nli
Retriever for the pipeline pass: search_bge_ft (top-1)

Label distribution in dev: SUPPORT 124 / CONTRADICT 64 / NEI 112
Majority-class baseline (always SUPPORT): 0.413 accuracy

===== pipeline (retrieved evidence) =====
Accuracy: 0.543  (163/300)
gold \ pred        SUPPORT  CONTRADICT         NEI
SUPPORT                 46           3          75
CONTRADICT               6          15          43
NEI                      5           5         102
class            precision      recall          f1
SUPPORT              0.807       0.371       0.508
CONTRADICT           0.652       0.234       0.345
NEI                  0.464       0.911       0.614
Macro-F1: 0.489

===== nli only (gold evidence) =====
Accuracy: 0.560  (168/300)
gold \ pred        SUPPORT  CONTRADICT         NEI
SUPPORT                 53           3          68
CONTRADICT               7          16          41
NEI                      6           7          99
class            precision      recall          f1
SUPPORT              0.803       0.427       0.558
CONTRADICT           0.615       0.250       0.356
NEI                  0.476       0.884       0.619
Macro-F1: 0.511

Notes:
- Beats the majority baseline (0.543 vs 0.413).
- Retrieval is NOT the bottleneck: gold evidence only lifts accuracy 0.543 -> 0.560.
  The NLI model itself is the limiting factor.
- The model over-predicts NEI (recall 0.88-0.91) and under-recalls SUPPORT (0.37-0.43)
  and CONTRADICT (0.23-0.25). Fine-tuning on SciFact should mainly help those two.
